#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:6
msgid "Internal Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:8
msgid ""
"A common pattern for implementing complex macros is to define helper arms "
"(often called **internal rules**) prefixed with a unique, non-standard "
"token, such as `@`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:12
msgid ""
"These internal arms are not meant to be called by users, but are used "
"internally by the macro's public entry points to delegate and reuse logic:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:16
msgid "// Copyright 2026 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:17
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:20
msgid "// Internal helper rules:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:22
msgid "\"all-lit: {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:25
msgid "\"some-lit: {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:28
msgid "// Public entrypoints:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:38
#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:39
msgid "\"format: {} {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:38
msgid "\"wow\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:39
msgid "\"non-literal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:46
msgid ""
"Note that `@` is purely a convention, which works well because `@` cannot "
"begin a standard Rust item or expression, ensuring public users don't "
"accidentally invoke these helper arms."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/internal-rules.md:49
msgid ""
"Trace the public matcher arms' flow through the recursive call to "
"(`print_literals!`) while selecting the next branch to take using the `@`\\-"
"prefixed tokens."
msgstr ""
